--   Pull through a uniform block expansion
-- statement:
--   **Pull through a uniform block expansion.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFSLift`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFS.pull_flatMap (sh : Shape) (g : List ℕ → List ℕ) (hg : ∀ a, Valid sh a → Valid sh (g a))
--       (f : α → List β) (B : ℕ) (hf : ∀ x, (f x).length = B) (d : α) (d' : β)
--       (xs : List α) (hxs : xs.length = vol sh) :
--       (AModel.pull sh sh g d xs).flatMap f =
--         AModel.pull (sh ++ [B]) (sh ++ [B]) (fun a => g (a.take sh.length) ++ a.drop sh.length) d'
--           (xs.flatMap f)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFS §1: lifting a pull through a fixed-length item expansion*: If every item `x` of an array of shape `sh` is expanded into a block `f x` of `B` entries
--   (`bitsL w` = `flatMap (encW w)` with `B = w + 1`, or `gflat` with `B = 2`), the expanded array
--   has shape `sh ++ [B]`, and a pull on `sh` becomes the pull on `sh ++ [B]` that acts on the first
--   `sh.length` digits and fixes the last one (`pull_flatMap`).  For the field swap `swapPos p q`
--   (`p, q < sh.length`) this is again `swapPos p q` (`pull_swapPos_flatMap`).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** This lemma belongs to the item-language (IL) layer of the integer-multiplication-kappa campaign: tape-level programs (register programs over 64 item stacks of the `NLogN` multitape framework, definition bundles `IntMul_HvdH_M_Defs1`–`IntMul_HvdH_M_Defs8`) that implement the data-movement primitives of the OpenAI preprint *Integer multiplication below $n\log n$* (field moves, row split/merge, shifts, the uniform Proposition 11 interchange, Lemma 12 with fine $O(1)$-per-element costs, Gaussian record primitives, Proposition 14 pieces) with exact list denotations from the array-model bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*` and explicit cost bounds. All names refer to the definition bundles up to `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs18`.
